    {
      "id": "checklist",
      "audioPath": "video-production/understanding-contrasts/audio/checklist.m4a",
      "audioSeconds": 38.804807,
      "durationSeconds": 39.654807,
      "durationInFrames": 1190,
      "startSeconds": 257.253629,
      "startFrame": 7721
    }
  ],
  "cues": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "text": "A first-level model can contain several explanatory variables, but a scientific result usually begins with a narrower question.",
      "startSeconds": 0,
      "endSeconds": 6.767068945054945,
      "startFrame": 0,
      "endFrame": 204
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "text": "Was the response during left-button trials greater than the response during right-button trials?",
      "startSeconds": 6.767068945054945,
      "endSeconds": 11.654396516483516,
      "startFrame": 203,
      "endFrame": 350
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "text": "Was one condition positively related to the measured BOLD signal?",
      "startSeconds": 11.654396516483516,
      "endSeconds": 15.413879263736263,
      "startFrame": 349,
      "endFrame": 463
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "text": "A contrast turns a question like that into a precise set of weights.",
      "startSeconds": 15.413879263736263,
      "endSeconds": 20.301206835164834,
      "startFrame": 462,
      "endFrame": 610
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "text": "In this lesson, we will connect those weights to the parameter estimates in the general linear model, interpret baseline and difference contrasts, and identify the quality-control checks that prevent a correct calculation from answering the wrong question.",
      "startSeconds": 20.301206835164834,
      "endSeconds": 34.211293,
      "startFrame": 609,
      "endFrame": 1027
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "text": "At each voxel, FEAT fits the general linear model.",
      "startSeconds": 35.061293,
      "endSeconds": 38.5369846,
      "startFrame": 1051,
      "endFrame": 1157
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "text": "The design matrix contains the explanatory variables, or EVs, and beta contains one estimated coefficient for each model column.",
      "startSeconds": 38.5369846,
      "endSeconds": 45.87455575555555,
      "startFrame": 1156,
      "endFrame": 1377
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "text": "Those coefficients describe how strongly each predictor contributes to the observed signal after accounting for the other predictors.",
      "startSeconds": 45.874555755555555,
      "endSeconds": 52.82593895555556,
      "startFrame": 1376,
      "endFrame": 1585
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "text": "A contrast does not refit the model and does not change the original beta estimates.",
      "startSeconds": 52.82593895555556,
      "endSeconds": 58.61875828888889,
      "startFrame": 1584,
      "endFrame": 1759
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "text": "Instead, it defines a linear combination of selected estimates.",
      "startSeconds": 58.618758288888884,
      "endSeconds": 62.09444988888888,
      "startFrame": 1758,
      "endFrame": 1863
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "text": "In compact notation, the contrast estimate is c transpose beta.",
      "startSeconds": 62.09444988888889,
      "endSeconds": 65.95632944444445,
      "startFrame": 1862,
      "endFrame": 1979
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "text": "The vector c contains the weights that encode the hypothesis.",
      "startSeconds": 65.95632944444444,
      "endSeconds": 69.818209,
      "startFrame": 1978,
      "endFrame": 2095
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "text": "Suppose the original EV order is Left followed by Right.",
      "startSeconds": 70.66820899999999,
      "endSeconds": 74.16962282608695,
      "startFrame": 2120,
      "endFrame": 2226
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "text": "The contrast one, zero selects the Left coefficient.",
      "startSeconds": 74.16962282608695,
      "endSeconds": 76.97075388695652,
      "startFrame": 2225,
      "endFrame": 2310
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "text": "In the usual FEAT task model, it tests a positive Left effect relative to the implicit baseline represented by the rest of the model.",
      "startSeconds": 76.97075388695652,
      "endSeconds": 85.37414706956521,
      "startFrame": 2309,
      "endFrame": 2562
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "text": "Zero, one selects the Right coefficient.",
      "startSeconds": 85.37414706956521,
      "endSeconds": 87.47499536521738,
      "startFrame": 2561,
      "endFrame": 2625
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "text": "These are not direct comparisons between Left and Right.",
      "startSeconds": 87.47499536521738,
      "endSeconds": 90.62626780869564,
      "startFrame": 2624,
      "endFrame": 2719
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "text": "They ask whether each selected estimate is positive in its modeled context.",
      "startSeconds": 90.62626780869564,
      "endSeconds": 94.82796439999998,
      "startFrame": 2718,
      "endFrame": 2845
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "text": "A contrast using one, one tests the positive sum of the two coefficients.",
      "startSeconds": 94.82796439999998,
      "endSeconds": 99.37980237391302,
      "startFrame": 2844,
      "endFrame": 2982
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "text": "Using one half, one half gives their numerical average.",
      "startSeconds": 99.37980237391304,
      "endSeconds": 102.5310748173913,
      "startFrame": 2981,
      "endFrame": 3076
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "text": "Those scaled contrasts have the same t or z statistic, but their cope values are on different scales, so name and report them carefully.",
      "startSeconds": 102.5310748173913,
      "endSeconds": 110.934468,
      "startFrame": 3075,
      "endFrame": 3329
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "text": "To compare Left directly with Right, use one, negative one.",
      "startSeconds": 111.78446799999999,
      "endSeconds": 115.40121843478259,
      "startFrame": 3353,
      "endFrame": 3463
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "text": "This computes beta Left minus beta Right.",
      "startSeconds": 115.40121843478259,
      "endSeconds": 117.93294373913042,
      "startFrame": 3462,
      "endFrame": 3538
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "text": "The null hypothesis is that the weighted difference equals zero, and the positive direction tests whether Left is greater than Right.",
      "startSeconds": 117.93294373913042,
      "endSeconds": 125.5281196521739,
      "startFrame": 3537,
      "endFrame": 3766
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "text": "Reversing the signs gives negative one, one, which tests Right greater than Left.",
      "startSeconds": 125.5281196521739,
      "endSeconds": 130.2298952173913,
      "startFrame": 3765,
      "endFrame": 3907
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "text": "A negative weight does not mean deactivation.",
      "startSeconds": 130.2298952173913,
      "endSeconds": 132.7616205217391,
      "startFrame": 3906,
      "endFrame": 3983
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "text": "It means that the corresponding coefficient is subtracted in this particular hypothesis.",
      "startSeconds": 132.76162052173913,
      "endSeconds": 137.10172104347825,
      "startFrame": 3982,
      "endFrame": 4114
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "text": "Direction matters: Left greater than Right and Right greater than Left are related, but they are not interchangeable labels for one contrast.",
      "startSeconds": 137.10172104347825,
      "endSeconds": 145.058572,
      "startFrame": 4113,
      "endFrame": 4352
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "text": "Contrast numbers only have meaning when they are aligned with the correct design-matrix columns.",
      "startSeconds": 145.908572,
      "endSeconds": 151.13576555319148,
      "startFrame": 4377,
      "endFrame": 4535
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "text": "If the actual order is Right then Left, the weights one, negative one test Right greater than Left, even if the contrast is named Left greater than Right.",
      "startSeconds": 151.13576555319148,
      "endSeconds": 161.59015265957444,
      "startFrame": 4534,
      "endFrame": 4848
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "text": "Before running FEAT, write the EV order, read each contrast as a sentence, and point from every weight to its displayed column name.",
      "startSeconds": 161.59015265957447,
      "endSeconds": 170.1776849255319,
      "startFrame": 4847,
      "endFrame": 5106
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "text": "Then inspect the design preview.",
      "startSeconds": 170.1776849255319,
      "endSeconds": 172.04453976595744,
      "startFrame": 5105,
      "endFrame": 5162
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "text": "Empty columns, swapped timing files, duplicated predictors, or unexpected derivatives can all change the interpretation.",
      "startSeconds": 172.04453976595744,
      "endSeconds": 177.64510428723403,
      "startFrame": 5161,
      "endFrame": 5330
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "text": "A plausible activation map cannot repair a mislabeled hypothesis.",
      "startSeconds": 177.64510428723403,
      "endSeconds": 181.00544299999999,
      "startFrame": 5329,
      "endFrame": 5431
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "text": "In FEAT, open Full model setup and then Contrasts and F-tests.",
      "startSeconds": 181.85544299999998,
      "endSeconds": 185.88280095604392,
      "startFrame": 5455,
      "endFrame": 5577
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "text": "Give each contrast a scientific name rather than a generic number.",
      "startSeconds": 185.88280095604392,
      "endSeconds": 189.91015891208787,
      "startFrame": 5576,
      "endFrame": 5698
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "text": "Enter the weights in the displayed EV order.",
      "startSeconds": 189.9101589120879,
      "endSeconds": 192.8391465164835,
      "startFrame": 5697,
      "endFrame": 5786
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "text": "For the source lab, the model contains Left and Right EVs, followed by contrasts for each condition, both directional differences, and a combined positive effect.",
      "startSeconds": 192.8391465164835,
      "endSeconds": 201.99223278021978,
      "startFrame": 5785,
      "endFrame": 6060
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "text": "The screenshot here is evidence from the real teaching workflow, not a generated interface.",
      "startSeconds": 201.99223278021975,
      "endSeconds": 207.11796108791205,
      "startFrame": 6059,
      "endFrame": 6214
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "text": "Before selecting Done, compare every row with the approved analysis plan and save the design file so the model specification remains reproducible.",
      "startSeconds": 207.11796108791208,
      "endSeconds": 215.172677,
      "startFrame": 6213,
      "endFrame": 6456
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "text": "For each contrast, FEAT writes several related outputs.",
      "startSeconds": 216.022677,
      "endSeconds": 219.31908124489794,
      "startFrame": 6480,
      "endFrame": 6580
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "text": "The cope is the contrast of parameter estimates: the weighted effect in the units of the model.",
      "startSeconds": 219.31908124489794,
      "endSeconds": 226.3239402653061,
      "startFrame": 6579,
      "endFrame": 6790
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "text": "The varcope describes uncertainty in that contrast estimate.",
      "startSeconds": 226.3239402653061,
      "endSeconds": 229.62034451020406,
      "startFrame": 6789,
      "endFrame": 6889
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "text": "Dividing the cope by its standard error produces a t statistic, which FEAT converts to a z statistic for inference and reporting.",
      "startSeconds": 229.62034451020406,
      "endSeconds": 238.68545618367347,
      "startFrame": 6888,
      "endFrame": 7161
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "text": "A z-statistic map is therefore standardized evidence, not an effect-size map.",
      "startSeconds": 238.68545618367347,
      "endSeconds": 243.21801202040817,
      "startFrame": 7160,
      "endFrame": 7297
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "text": "Higher-level analyses use the cope together with its varcope.",
      "startSeconds": 243.21801202040814,
      "endSeconds": 246.92646679591834,
      "startFrame": 7296,
      "endFrame": 7408
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "text": "Thresholded z-statistic images help visualize inferential results, but interpretation should begin only after checking preprocessing, registration, the design matrix, and the contrast definition.",
      "startSeconds": 246.92646679591837,
      "endSeconds": 256.403629,
      "startFrame": 7407,
      "endFrame": 7693
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "text": "Before you run FEAT, complete five checks.",
      "startSeconds": 257.253629,
      "endSeconds": 260.08314617708334,
      "startFrame": 7717,
      "endFrame": 7803
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "text": "First, list EVs in matrix order.",
      "startSeconds": 260.08314617708334,
      "endSeconds": 262.50844661458336,
      "startFrame": 7802,
      "endFrame": 7876
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "text": "Second, state the scientific question for every contrast.",
      "startSeconds": 262.5084466145833,
      "endSeconds": 265.74218053124997,
      "startFrame": 7875,
      "endFrame": 7973
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "text": "Third, translate the sentence into weights and then translate the weights back into a sentence.",
      "startSeconds": 265.74218053124997,
      "endSeconds": 271.805431625,
      "startFrame": 7972,
      "endFrame": 8155
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "text": "Fourth, inspect the design matrix and contrast arrows visually.",
      "startSeconds": 271.805431625,
      "endSeconds": 275.44338228124997,
      "startFrame": 8154,
      "endFrame": 8264
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "text": "Fifth, distinguish the effect estimate, its uncertainty, and the standardized statistic you will later report.",
      "startSeconds": 275.44338228124997,
      "endSeconds": 281.506633375,
      "startFrame": 8263,
      "endFrame": 8446
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "text": "If the design, weights, and scientific language tell the same story, the contrast is ready to run.",
      "startSeconds": 281.506633375,
      "endSeconds": 288.3783179479166,
      "startFrame": 8445,
      "endFrame": 8652
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "text": "Next, the hands-on walkthrough will configure these contrasts in a live Neurodesk session and inspect the corresponding FEAT outputs.",
      "startSeconds": 288.3783179479166,
      "endSeconds": 296.058436,
      "startFrame": 8651,
      "endFrame": 8882
    }
  ]
}
